Band Description:

Static Hydrometer is a five-member electro-acoustic dance ensemble built around long glass harmonies and rapidly evolving guitar interlock.

Élodie Marais — glass armonica, friction-bloom harmony, bowl voicing, overtone control.
Pascal Ilunga — lead soukous guitar, sebene figures, high-register arpeggios.
Mireille Kanku — counter-guitar, clipped triads, displaced rhythmic cells.
Jonas Declerq — prepared electric bass, damped low punctuation, sparse pickups.
Chantal Mbala — likembe, shaker, compact repeating cells, rhythmic anchor.

Live drums are performed by rotating collaborators, but the core five remain responsible for the compositional structure. There is no conventional frontperson. Élodie defines the slow harmonic reservoir while Pascal and Mireille generate motion around it. Jonas controls low-frequency space, and Chantal supplies small fixed coordinates that prevent the interlocking guitars from drifting apart.

